<title>USA: U.S. September PPI energy goods prices.</title>
<headline>U.S. September PPI energy goods prices.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>- The U.S. Labor Department reported energy components of the producer price index as follows, with comparisons (1982=100 unless stated otherwise).</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				Sept    Aug   Sept96/95</p>
<p> Finished Energy Goods     0.2    0.7     7.1</p>
<p> -Gasoline		     0.9    0.9    14.2</p>
<p> -Heating Oil		  2.0    4.1    25.3</p>
<p> -Residential Gas-Y	 -2.1    0.7     6.0</p>
<p>Y-Dec 1990=100.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				Sept    Aug   Sept96/95</p>
<p> Intermed.Energy Goods     0.8    0.9     8.9</p>
<p> -Liq.Petroleum Gas-Z	0.1    5.0    25.3</p>
<p> -Jet Fuel		     6.8    3.0    29.9</p>
<p> -Diesel Fuel		  0.4   Unch    25.8</p>
<p> -Residual Fuel-Z	    0.2   -0.3    32.9</p>
<p>Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				Sept    Aug   Sept96/95</p>
<p> Crude Energy Materials-Y  0.6    0.7    20.9</p>
<p> -Coal-Z			 3.1    0.1     1.4</p>
<p> -Nat.Gas to Pipelines-Z  -6.4   -1.2    28.0</p>
<p> -Petroleum-Z		  7.3    3.2    28.6</p>
<p>Y-Includes crude petroleum. Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
</text>
